  "prompt_text": "The figure is a schematic of a cryogenic electrical metrology setup that links a device under test to quantum voltage and resistance standards. The central element is a Hall-bar–like chip operated at very low temperature, labeled around 10 mK, with a transverse voltage \\(V_{yx}\\) measured across contacts on the sample. Current \\(I\\) from the device under test is routed through the measurement circuit, and a null detector \\(V_{\\text{null}}\\) is used to balance or compare voltages rather than measuring them directly.\n\nAbove the sample, a separate module at about 4 K contains a Josephson-junction array, indicated by repeated crossed symbols and the label \\(V_J\\). This serves as the voltage standard. The lower, colder chip acts as the resistance standard, apparently based on a quantized Hall device, since the measured quantity is a Hall voltage across a patterned bar structure.\n\nColored wiring distinguishes the two comparison paths: one connecting the sample to the null detector and another to the device under test. Overall, the diagram shows a precision bridge arrangement in which a quantum Hall resistance standard and a Josephson voltage standard are combined in a single low-temperature measurement chain.",
